[20.1777, "o", "host: Linux x86_64\r\n\r\n== 1. Control groups (cgroups)\r\n"]
[20.1789, "o", "  PASS  cgroup v2 is in use (cgroup2fs)\r\n"]
[20.1795, "o", "\r\n== 2. Podman (the container engine)\r\n"]
[20.1952, "o", "  PASS  podman found: podman version 5.8.7\r\n"]
[20.197, "o", "        major version 5 is supported\r\n"]
[20.2888, "o", "  PASS  podman runs rootless (recommended)\r\n\r\n== 3. Rootless user-id mapping (newuidmap / subuid / subgid)\r\n"]
[20.2895, "o", "  PASS  newuidmap found: /usr/bin/newuidmap\r\n"]
[20.2914, "o", "  PASS  /etc/subuid has an entry for youruser\r\n"]
[20.2936, "o", "  PASS  /etc/subgid has an entry for youruser\r\n\r\n== 4. SELinux (Linux only)\r\n"]
[20.2956, "o", "  PASS  SELinux is Enforcing - this is the well-tested case\r\n        You do NOT need: setsebool container_manage_cgroup, /etc/containers/policy.json edits,\r\n"]
[20.2962, "o", "        or --security-opt label=disable. Podman labels systemd containers container_init_t.\r\n\r\n== 5. Python (Molecule needs Python 3.10 or newer)\r\n"]
[20.3076, "o", "  PASS  python3 found: 3.14\r\n"]
[20.3084, "o", "  PASS  python3 is new enough (need >= 3.10)\r\n\r\n== 6. Molecule and the Podman driver\r\n"]
[21.1286, "o", "  PASS  molecule \u001b[32m26.9.0\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[21.3488, "o", "  PASS  the 'podman' driver is available (from molecule-plugins)\r\n\r\n== 7. The containers.podman Ansible collection\r\n"]
[21.9736, "o", "  PASS  containers.podman collection is installed (version 1.20.2)\r\n\r\n----------------------------------------\r\nRESULT: READY - every check passed\r\n"]
